  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Preheat oven to 240°C/220°C fan-forced.\n• Cut potato into fries and place on the lined oven tray. Season with salt and drizzle with olive oil.\n• Toss to coat and bake until tender, 20-25 mins.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/6a4cc53e746dd895cd0b3df6/step-1eab4100.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Meanwhile, in a shallow bowl, add the plain flour. In a second shallow bowl, whisk egg. In a third shallow bowl, combine panko breadcrumbs (see ingredients) and sesame seeds.\n• Dip Japanese tofu pieces into the flour to coat, then into egg and finally in breadcrumb mixture. Set aside on a plate.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/6a4cc53e746dd895cd0b3df6/step-ee2cc610.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• In a large frying pan, heat enough olive oil to coat the base over medium-high heat.\n• Cook crumbed tofu until golden and cooked through, 2-4 mins each side. (Cook in batches if your pan is getting crowded or add extra oil if needed so the tofu does not stick to the pan).\n• Transfer to a paper towel-lined plate.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/6a4cc53e746dd895cd0b3df6/step-93d85920.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Meanwhile, halve continental rolls and bake directly on a wire oven rack until heated through, 2-3 mins.\n• In a medium bowl, combine mixed salad leaves and a drizzle of vinegar.\n• Spread rolls with the mayonnaise and sweet chilli sauce. Top with crumbed tofu and salad leaves.\n• Serve with fries.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/6a4cc53e746dd895cd0b3df6/step-9c867230.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
